  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research on biodigesters in Senegal and stakeholder analysis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This study evaluated the current state of biodigesters in Senegal, mapping organic matter availability, market players, and barriers to scaling the sector. The research includes a feasibility assessment of biodigester expansion, an analysis of access and deployment across different population segments, and a stakeholder mapping exercise. The findings informed discussions during the multi-stakeholder strategy week in November 2024, and supported the Dutch Embassy in shaping its engagement in waste-to-energy. The study also aimed to identify potential Dutch interventions in trade, diplomacy, and knowledge exchange to contribute to Senegal&#x2019;s energy transition and waste management goals.</narrative>
  </description>
